Centering a `div` in CSS can be done in several ways depending on whether you want to center it horizontally, vertically, or both. Below are some common methods:

### 1. Centering Horizontally

If you just need to center a `div` horizontally within its parent container, you can use the following method:

```css
.parent {
    text-align: center; /* This will center inline and inline-block elements */
}

.child {
    display: inline-block;
}
```

Or if your child element has a fixed width:

```css
.parent {
    text-align: center;
}

.child {
    margin-left: auto;
    margin-right: auto;
    width: 200px; /* Fixed width */
}
